  "vetoes": [
    "Three actual hand renders remain materially below the source: collapsed/faceted curls in v1; smooth uncreased surface and implausible pinch/contact in v2/v3. Nails and dark material do not restore anatomy or deformation quality.",
    "The final phone holding frame crops the thumb while the remaining fingers hover across the bowl. This does not preserve a believable grasp; the complete page is not authorized."
  ],
  "finding": "Cork and roasted bean detail improved in the bounded material finish, but the hand still reads as a smooth game prop and lacks the source anatomy and natural local articulation. No average across the other materials may compensate for this core loss.",
  "nextAction": "reject-current-asset-plan-and-select-another-supported-reference",
